<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">Overall health market share — unverified third-party figure:</span> The 5.31% GDPI-based overall health market share could <b>not</b> be located in any Niva Bupa company-published document (annual report, investor presentation, press release, or earnings call transcript) despite extensive searching. It is sourced from Screener.in, a third-party aggregator <doc_source>step31web1</doc_source>, and should be treated as indicative rather than company-confirmed. Niva Bupa's own filings consistently disclose only the <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">Retail Health Market Share (9.4%, FY25)</span> as their headline positioning metric.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">IFRS expense ratio — not disclosed:</span> Niva Bupa does not separately publish an IFRS expense ratio. The presentation shows only the Combined Insurance Service Ratio (103.0%) and IFRS claims ratio (63.8%) for FY25. A residual of ~39.2% could be back-calculated, but per strict data-integrity rules, no estimated value has been entered.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #1E3A8A;background:#EFF6FF;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="color:#1E3A8A;font-weight:600">Source coverage:</span> The standalone FY2024-25 Annual Report PDF could not be located on Niva Bupa's investor relations site at the time of this extract (only the FY2023-24 Annual Report was accessible). All FY25 data above is therefore drawn from the audited-results-linked Investor Presentation, Press Release, and Q4 FY25 Earnings Call Transcript, all published on <b>2025-05-07</b> — representing the company's primary disclosures for the FY25 audited results.
</div>

**Suggested follow-ups:** If you need the like-for-like ("without 1/n") growth-adjusted ratios for trend comparison against FY24, or once the formal FY2024-25 Annual Report is published, I can cross-check and update the GWP, ratio, and market-share figures against that primary filing.</ans>
